& [ParticipantIdentityRecordContract] is the record contract for a participant in a multi-user and multi-agent collaboration surface
  + [participant_uuid] is required stable UUID for the participant record
  + [participant_kind] is exclusive ParticipantKind
  + [display_name] is projection label only
  + [principal_ref] is optional external identity reference
  + [conversation_uuid_set] is set of conversation_uuid values where the participant is visible
  + [agent_instance_ref] is optional local agent instance reference
  + [surface_presence_set] is set of surface_projection references where participant visibility is projected
  + [authority_class_set] is set of AuthorityClass values granted by accepted source authority
  + [authority_basis_set] is set of source_document, canonical_specification, or signed_review references
  + [freshness_state] is current, stale, blocked, contradicted, or unknown
  + [revocation_state] is active, revoked, expired, superseded, or unknown

  = must: treat participant_uuid as an identity key, not permission by itself
  = must: require authority_basis_set before a participant may claim any authority_class beyond surface_projection or carrier_notice
  = must: mark generated or inferred participant records as projection-only until source-preserved authority accepts them
  = must: keep display_name non-authoritative
  - never: use participant_kind agent, manager_agent, or worker_agent as assignment or dispatch authority
  - never: use principal_ref or surface presence as credential access permission

& [ConversationIdentityRecordContract] is the record contract for a durable collaboration conversation
  + [conversation_uuid] is required stable UUID for the conversation lineage
  + [conversation_purpose] is narrative description of the bounded collaboration purpose
  + [source_authority_ref_set] is set of source_document or canonical_specification references that may steer the conversation
  + [surface_projection_set] is set of conversation surface projections
  + [carrier_notice_set] is set of mailbox, IRC, Matrix, web, terminal, Codex, browser, Langflow, narrative, or debug carrier notices
  + [participant_set] is set of participant_uuid references
  + [active_claim_set] is set of coordination_claim references
  + [work_packet_candidate_set] is set of packet candidates visible to the conversation
  + [operation_request_set] is set of dry-run operation request references visible to the conversation
  + [read_cursor_set] is set of carrier read cursor projections
  + [freshness_state] is current, stale, blocked, contradicted, or unknown
  + [lineage_state] is root, branch, merge_candidate, superseded, archived, or unknown

  = must: treat conversation_uuid as the durable handle for narrative and coordination continuity
  = must: preserve source_authority_ref_set separately from carrier_notice_set
  = must: distinguish conversation branch, conversation projection, and surface thread
  = must: make stale carrier notices visible without promoting them to source authority
  - never: treat IRC room, Matrix room, web thread, terminal scrollback, Codex thread, mailbox inbox, Langflow graph, or browser page as canonical memory by itself

& [SurfaceProjectionIdentityContract] is the identity contract for a surface-specific projection of a conversation
  + [surface_projection_uuid] is required stable UUID for the projection record
  + [conversation_uuid] is required parent conversation identity
  + [surface_kind] is exclusive ConversationSurfaceKind
  + [surface_address] is projection-specific address or label
  + [projected_record_set] is set of projected source, narrative, claim, packet, or operation references
  + [authority_notice] is required projection notice explaining non-authoritative status
  + [freshness_notice] is required projection notice explaining current, stale, blocked, contradicted, or unknown state
  + [inbound_action_policy] is accepted, refused, queued_for_source_preserving_intake, or unknown

  = must: require authority_notice and freshness_notice on every decision-making projection
  = must: classify inbound actions before they can affect source, claims, work packets, operations, or reviews
  = must: route source-changing inbound actions through source-preserving intake and SJS governance
  - never: let a surface projection mutate canonical authority directly
  - never: let inbound_action_policy accepted mean dispatch, operations control, or live control

& [AuthorityClassPromotionContract] is the rule for moving a record between authority classes
  + [from_class] is AuthorityClass
  + [to_class] is AuthorityClass
  + [promotion_basis] is source_document, canonical_specification, signed_review, or explicit human override record
  + [promotion_review] is required for any promotion that affects claims, packets, operations, assignment, dispatch, or live control
  + [promotion_state] is proposed, accepted, refused, stale, superseded, or blocked

  = must: require signed source-preserved authority before promoting surface_projection, carrier_notice, narrative_record, generated_output, work_packet_candidate, operation_request, dry_run_result, or human_approval_display into a stronger authority class
  = must: require separate future SJS authority before any promotion to dispatch_authority or live_control_authority
  = must: require completion review for every accepted promotion that changes slice readiness
  - never: promote generated_output to source_document
  - never: promote carrier_notice to canonical_specification
  - never: promote work_packet_candidate to dispatch_authority
  - never: promote dry_run_result to human_approval_display or live_control_authority
  - never: promote human_approval_display to live_control_authority without explicit future safety authority, freshness, revocation, rollback, monitor, and emergency-stop proof

& [AuthorityClassPermissionMatrix] is the planning matrix for allowed and refused authority behavior
  + [source_document] may support canonical_specification through SJS processing only
  + [canonical_specification] may open signed_review and slice readiness through completion review
  + [signed_review] may open the next gated planning slice only within its stated scope
  + [narrative_record] may support reentry and context but may not authorize implementation or dispatch
  + [surface_projection] may display source state, projection state, freshness, and notices but may not mutate authority directly
  + [carrier_notice] may carry coordination information but may not become signed authority
  + [coordination_claim] may declare intent and work boundary but may not assign or dispatch work
  + [assignment_candidate] may suggest a responsible participant but may not command action
  + [work_packet_candidate] may package bounded work context but may not dispatch an agent or job
  + [operation_request] may request dry-run consideration but may not execute an operation
  + [dry_run_result] may inform planning and refusal but may not approve live action
  + [human_approval_display] may show approval state but may not substitute for future safety authority
  + [generated_output] may support fixture comparison but may not become source or canonical authority
  + [dispatch_authority] is absent and blocked in current scope
  + [live_control_authority] is absent and blocked in current scope

  = must: expose refused promotions as operational faults when attempted
  = must: preserve blocked authority classes visibly so downstream planning does not infer false readiness

